{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1534618-v20-flaw-dulled-bite","id":1534618,"title":"[V20] Flaw: Dulled Bite","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-23T22:24:14-07:00","id":1534618,"title":"[V20] Flaw: Dulled Bite","content":"Can anybody explain to me how this flaw is supposed to work RAW?<br /> <br /> Specifically this part:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When feeding, you need to find some other method of making the blood flow. Failing that, you <b>must achieve double the normal number of successes</b> in order to make your bite penetrate properly. </div> </div> </div>To what role is that referring, and how many success would someone with that flaw would need at that role?<br /> <br /> Btw. it is also a bit wired that the flaw says nothing about the bite damage...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T22:44:51-07:00","id":1534620,"title":"","content":"In VDA20, biting is a combat maneuver requiring a clinch or hold or tackle first to be performed, and then a roll of Dexterity+Brawl+1. If successful, the biter can choose whether to inflict damage or suck blood.<br /> If the same is true in V20, I would assume that it's the Dexterity+Brawl+1 roll, but it's admittedly ambiguous and weird.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":". 04-24-2024, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T00:25:23-07:00","id":1534623,"title":"","content":"OK but does that mean you just need 2 (net-)success on the attack role to suck blood in combat instead of 1?<br /> <br /> That would still mean that the Flaw would have no effect for regular feeding out of combat, where you afaik don't role for attack, and no effect if you bite in combat to do damage instead of to suck blood...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T05:50:45-07:00","id":1534629,"title":"","content":"This is where logic comes in the picture<br /> With a normal human set of teeth it is not that easy to pierce the skin without tearing or bitung out a chunk of flesh<br /> The fangs leave two neat little holes to drink from<br /> The flaw is more combat related , with the bite-attack rules<br /> During hunt, you don't really roll you managed to bite or not","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"